WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:01.480
Franchises are inescapable.

00:00:01.480 --> 00:00:07.069
The endless-sequel format works well, with
blockbusters like Star Wars and the Fast and

00:00:07.069 --> 00:00:09.929
Furious movies able to make hits with every
release.

00:00:09.929 --> 00:00:13.940
But there are some movies out there that would
maybe just be better off left alone.

00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:18.550
Whether the first films were standalone greats
or bargain-bin flops, here are some upcoming

00:00:18.550 --> 00:00:21.400
sequels that we just can’t believe are being
made.

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:22.550
Wedding Crashers 2

00:00:22.550 --> 00:00:28.189
The 2005 hit Wedding Crashers is finally ready
to crash theaters again in the form of a sequel,

00:00:28.189 --> 00:00:29.539
according to Variety.

00:00:29.539 --> 00:00:35.260
The original grossed over $200 million domestically
over a decade ago, and now Wedding Crashers

00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:40.620
director David Dobkin is laying the groundwork
for a sequel that could include 007 himself,

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:41.630
Daniel Craig.

00:00:41.630 --> 00:00:43.290
Dobkin wrote on Quora:

00:00:43.290 --> 00:00:47.469
"Vince, Owen and myself sat around at Owen's
house one day and broke the story.

00:00:47.469 --> 00:00:48.760
It was really funny.

00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:52.969
We wanted Daniel Craig to be the ultimate
wedding crasher, with his sexy body and his

00:00:52.969 --> 00:00:56.440
speedo, and the two guys would be incredibly
threatened by him."

00:00:58.190 --> 00:01:03.040
Provided Dobkin can tap into the same chemistry,
energy, and knockdown laughs the all-star

00:01:03.059 --> 00:01:07.680
cast summoned for the first film, this could
actually be a sequel worth waiting for.

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:13.830
Then again...fans hoped the same thing for
Zoolander 2, and look how that turned out.

00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:14.830
"Old?"

00:01:14.830 --> 00:01:15.830
"La-may?"

00:01:15.830 --> 00:01:16.900
Yes on both counts.

00:01:16.900 --> 00:01:18.650
American Pie 5

00:01:18.650 --> 00:01:22.990
Since 1999, the American Pie franchise has
given the world three additional servings

00:01:22.990 --> 00:01:25.710
of Jim, Oz, Finch, Michelle, and Stifler.

00:01:25.710 --> 00:01:31.260
And that’s not even counting the four straight-to-DVD
spin-offs, which were all pretty much, well…

00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:38.100
In the wake of 2012’s American Reunion,
the fourth theatrical installment of the franchise,

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:40.180
talk was already turning to a fifth film.

00:01:40.180 --> 00:01:45.900
In 2015, Tara Reid revealed that a fifth chapter
in the raunchy comedy saga was indeed in the

00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:48.700
works, and that "they may be doing it in Las
Vegas."

00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:53.390
And as surprising as it sounds, the franchise
might still actually be bankable — American

00:01:53.390 --> 00:01:57.460
Reunion brought in $234 million worldwide.

00:01:57.460 --> 00:01:59.180
Assassin's Creed 2

00:01:59.180 --> 00:02:03.030
Practically from the moment it hit theaters,
hype for Assassin’s Creed fell even harder

00:02:03.030 --> 00:02:05.200
than Michael Fassbender’s stunt double.

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:10.170
Even before the film opened, however, executive
producer Patrick Crowley told GameSpot that

00:02:10.170 --> 00:02:14.430
he fully expects to make Assassin’s Creed
the start of a film franchise, saying, "It's

00:02:14.430 --> 00:02:15.530
not a one-off.

00:02:15.530 --> 00:02:17.730
Everybody expects that this movie will continue."

00:02:17.730 --> 00:02:23.730
Star and producer Michael Fassbender also
told CinemaBlend in December 2016 that tentative

00:02:23.730 --> 00:02:28.700
plans were already laid out for a film trilogy:
"This is the sort of origin to this story.

00:02:28.700 --> 00:02:32.019
We have an idea of where he’s going to go
over the next two films.

00:02:32.019 --> 00:02:33.810
We kind of did a three-film arc."

00:02:33.810 --> 00:02:38.590
Both Fassbender and Crowley have been tight-lipped
about the sequel’s development ever since,

00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:42.379
but despite bombing in the domestic box office,
foreign ticket sales have launched Assassin’s

00:02:42.379 --> 00:02:48.310
Creed’s gross well past its production budget
of $125 million, making this sequel all the

00:02:48.310 --> 00:02:49.469
more likely.

00:02:49.469 --> 00:02:51.010
Gremlins 3

00:02:51.010 --> 00:02:55.579
More than 30 years after Gremlins arrived
in theaters — and more than 25 years after

00:02:55.579 --> 00:03:00.060
its follow-up, Gremlins 2: The New Batch,
underwhelmed at the box office — star Zach

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:04.040
Galligan has confirmed that Gremlins 3 has
been given the the go-ahead, along with an

00:03:04.040 --> 00:03:05.540
extra piece of good news:

00:03:05.540 --> 00:03:07.379
"It’s not going to be a reboot.

00:03:07.379 --> 00:03:10.219
It will not be a remake in any way, shape,
or form."

00:03:10.219 --> 00:03:14.930
The third installment in the franchise reportedly
has Steven Spielberg and original Gremlins

00:03:14.930 --> 00:03:20.129
screenwriter Chris Columbus attached, and
Carl Ellsworth, who wrote Disturbia, Red Dawn,

00:03:20.129 --> 00:03:23.519
and The Last House On The Left, is on board
to write the script.

00:03:23.519 --> 00:03:27.340
All that aside, rumors have been swirling
about a third Gremlins for years.

00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:29.499
We'll see if it actually happens this time.

00:03:29.499 --> 00:03:31.220
Goon: The Last of the Enforcers

00:03:31.220 --> 00:03:36.129
Goon: The Last of The Enforcers is a follow-up
to Goon, starring Seann William Scott with

00:03:36.129 --> 00:03:40.849
a supporting cast that boasts Liev Schreiber,
Elisha Cuthbert, and Wyatt Russell.

00:03:40.849 --> 00:03:45.489
Jay Baruchel, who also played a supporting
role in the original, has signed on to direct

00:03:45.489 --> 00:03:46.489
the sequel.

00:03:46.489 --> 00:03:51.000
Baruchel told Metro News Toronto he’s taking
the job seriously and doesn't want to let

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:52.140
Goon fans down.

00:03:52.140 --> 00:03:56.170
"You have no choice but to give them something
that you think is better than the first movie.

00:03:56.170 --> 00:03:59.650
So that's why it took five years between the
first two movies, is because we wanted to

00:03:59.650 --> 00:04:01.290
make sure we got it right."

00:04:01.290 --> 00:04:02.879
Zombieland 2

00:04:02.879 --> 00:04:10.430
It's the return of the double-tap.

00:04:10.430 --> 00:04:16.090
In late 2016, Deadpool writers Paul Wernick
and Rhett Reese revealed to Kevin Smith on

00:04:16.090 --> 00:04:20.709
Geeking Out that they received backing to
pursue a sequel to their surprise hit.

00:04:20.709 --> 00:04:25.910
A Zombieland sequel has been discussed numerous
times since the original racked up over $100

00:04:25.910 --> 00:04:31.090
million during its 2009 box office run, but
those talks have obviously all come to naught

00:04:31.090 --> 00:04:35.280
— so while Wernick and Reese's excitement
is infectious, we're still taking this with

00:04:35.280 --> 00:04:37.310
the teensiest grain of salt for now.

00:04:37.310 --> 00:04:38.850
Saw: Legacy

00:04:38.850 --> 00:04:41.440
This is the horror franchise that just won't
go away.

00:04:41.440 --> 00:04:44.200
Saw: Legacy will be the eighth installment
in the franchise.

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:49.260
That’s not exactly surprising, but since
the last one was called Saw 3D: The Final

00:04:49.260 --> 00:04:51.730
Chapter...well, we kind of hoped it really
was.

00:04:51.730 --> 00:04:55.870
While not much is known about the plot, it
seems safe to assume Saw: Legacy will involve

00:04:55.870 --> 00:04:59.490
a group of people being forced to play sadistic
games to stay alive.

00:04:59.490 --> 00:05:05.310
Michael and Peter Spierig directed, and it's
scheduled to drop October 27, 2017 — just

00:05:05.310 --> 00:05:06.870
in time for Halloween.

00:05:06.870 --> 00:05:07.870
The Predator

00:05:07.870 --> 00:05:12.670
After a long, painful run of cheesy cash-ins,
it’s about time we got a decent Predator

00:05:12.670 --> 00:05:17.660
movie, and Shane Black’s 2018 installment
— called simply The Predator — is already

00:05:17.660 --> 00:05:18.950
looking like a killer.

00:05:18.950 --> 00:05:23.970
Black, who wrote Lethal Weapon and directed
The Nice Guys, among plenty of other Hollywood

00:05:23.970 --> 00:05:28.300
classics, has been tapped to write and direct,
and he said he plans to push the franchise

00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:31.180
forward with a sequel rather than a reboot.

00:05:31.180 --> 00:05:35.060
Black — who actually played a bit part in
the original — told Collider he was reluctant

00:05:35.060 --> 00:05:38.930
to take the gig until Fox told him he'd have
enough money to deliver the movie he really

00:05:38.930 --> 00:05:40.060
wanted to make.

00:05:40.060 --> 00:05:44.390
Given Black's track record for quality with
action-packed blockbusters like Lethal Weapon

00:05:44.390 --> 00:05:46.820
and Iron Man 3, this bodes well.

00:05:46.820 --> 00:05:50.730
Frankly, the most unbelievable thing about
this sequel is that, after so many years,

00:05:50.730 --> 00:05:53.520
it might actually be completely awesome.

00:05:55.260 --> 00:05:56.180
"Stick around."

00:05:56.900 --> 00:05:57.760
Thanks for watching!

00:05:57.820 --> 00:06:00.280
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:02.600
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

